{"id":26257,"path":"/vocabulary/a1/common-verbs-and-verb-phrases-a1-english-vocabulary/","parentId":26178,"order":20,"section":"vocabulary","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Common verbs and verb phrases – A1 English Vocabulary","seo":{"title":"Common verbs and verb phrases – A1 English Vocabulary - Test-English","description":"Learn common verbs and verb phrases in English (Level A1) with pictures, examples, and interactive exercises with personalised feedback.","image":"/media/uploads/A1-English-Vocabulary_Common-verbs-and-verb-phrases.jpg"},"modified":"2023-10-11T08:11:01","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h2>Common Verbs and Verb Phrases</h2> <p>In this elementary <a href=\"/vocabulary\">vocabulary</a> lesson about Common Verbs and Verb Phrases, you will learn about common actions that we do in our everyday lives. Check the explanation and do the exercises.</p> <hr> <h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct options to complete these sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"927\"></div>","<h2>Common Verbs and Verb Phrases</h2> <h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct option for each gap.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"928\"></div>","<h2>Common Verbs and Verb Phrases</h2> <h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Write one word to complete each gap. Use the words in the box below.</h5> <p><span class=\"textBox\">cook – do – go(x2) – have – listen – play(x2) – read – watch</span><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"929\"></div> <p></p>","<h3>Exercise 4</h3> <h2>Common Verbs and Verb Phrases</h2> <h5>Match the sentences/pictures with the terms.</h5> <p></p> <h6>Reload the page to play again. Here’s a link to our <a href=\"https://quizlet.com/es/820021921/common-verbs-and-verb-phrases-a1-vocabulary-flash-cards/?i=4i1uip&amp;x=1jqt\">Quizlet study set</a> about Common Verbs and Verb Phrases.</h6>"],"explanation":"<h2>Common Verbs and Verb Phrases</h2> <p>In this A1 Elementary <a href=\"/vocabulary\">Vocabulary</a> Lesson, you will learn Common Verbs that we use every day. The pictures and examples below will help you understand and remember the terms.<br> <br> <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-26939\" src=\"/media/uploads/Common-verbs_A1-vocabulary.png\" alt=\"Infographic showing 20 common verbs and activities like 'call a friend' and 'cook dinner' for A1 English vocabulary.\" width=\"500\" height=\"1032\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h3>Example Sentences</h3> <ul class=\"vocab-ex\"> <li>She often <span class=\"numPink\">1</span> <span><strong>calls her friends</strong></span>.</li> <li>He never <span class=\"numPink\">2</span><strong><span> cooks dinner</span></strong>.</li> <li>She <span class=\"numPink\">3</span><strong><span> does exercise</span></strong> every day.</li> <li>(US) She <span class=\"numPink\">4</span> <span><strong>goes on vacation</strong></span> every summer. / (UK) She goes <span><strong>on holiday</strong> </span>every summer.</li> <li>She <span class=\"numPink\">5</span> <span><strong>goes to bed</strong> </span>at 10:30 pm.</li> <li>He <span class=\"numPink\">6</span> <span><strong>goes to work</strong></span> very early.</li> <li>For breakfast, she <span class=\"numPink\">7</span> <span><strong>drinks some coffee</strong></span>.</li> <li>She <span class=\"numPink\">8</span> <span><strong>eats dinner</strong></span> at 7 pm.</li> <li>She often <span class=\"numPink\">9</span> <span><strong>listens to music</strong></span>.</li> <li>He <span class=\"numPink\">10</span> <span><strong>plays football</strong></span> every weekend.</li> <li>She <span class=\"numPink\">11</span> <span><strong>plays the guitar</strong></span> as a hobby.</li> <li>He <span class=\"numPink\">12</span> <span><strong>plays video games</strong></span> every day.</li> <li>She <span class=\"numPink\">13</span> <span><strong>reads a book</strong></span> before going to bed.</li> <li>Sometimes she calls and sometimes she <span class=\"numPink\">14</span> <span><strong>sends a text</strong></span>.</li> <li>He <span class=\"numPink\">15</span> <span><strong>studies English</strong></span>.</li> <li>He often <span class=\"numPink\">16</span> <span><strong>takes photos</strong></span>.</li> <li>He is happy when he <span class=\"numPink\">17</span> <span><strong>visits a museum</strong></span>.</li> <li>He <span class=\"numPink\">18</span> <span><strong>watches TV</strong></span> after dinner.</li> <li>He <span class=\"numPink\">19</span> <span><strong>wears glasses</strong></span>.</li> <li>She <span class=\"numPink\">20</span> <span><strong>sends emails</strong></span> to all her friends.</li> </ul> <div class=\"noteblock\"> 🔍 <strong>Note</strong> that in the <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/present-simple/\">present simple</a> we add <strong>-s</strong> or <strong>-es</strong> at the end of the verb after <strong>he, she</strong> or <strong>it</strong>.</div> <h3>Listen &amp; Practice: Vocabulary with Pronunciation</h3> <p>Here’s a video to help you review the vocabulary from this lesson and improve your pronunciation.</p> <div class=\"video-container\"> <div class=\"embed-container\"><div data-youtube=\"ypSzRcPYUpo\"></div></div> </div> <div class=\"separator-dots\"><span>Flashcards</span></div> <p>After completing the exercises in this lesson on Common Verbs, you can use the unit’s <a href=\"https://quizlet.com/820021921\">Vocabulary Flashcards</a> to revise and help you memorize the terms.</p>","quizzes":[{"id":927,"questions":[{"id":7847,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> my friends to talk to them.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["drinks","listen","go","play","cook","call","goes","plays","work","do"]}]},{"id":7848,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>My wife and I always <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> dinner together.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["goes","do","call","drinks","plays","listen","cook","go","work","play"]}]},{"id":7849,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> exercise three times a week.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["listen","do","call","plays","cook","goes","drinks","work","play","go"]}]},{"id":7850,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> on vacation in the summer.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["drinks","plays","listen","go","play","cook","call","work","goes","do"]}]},{"id":7851,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>My wife <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to bed very early. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["listen","call","cook","do","goes","plays","go","drinks","work","play"]}]},{"id":7852,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I go to <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> by bus.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["listen","drinks","goes","plays","work","play","call","cook","go","do"]}]},{"id":7853,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>My wife always <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> a cup of coffee before work.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["plays","go","goes","cook","listen","work","drinks","call","do","play"]}]},{"id":7854,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the guitar in a band.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["drinks","cook","go","do","play","work","goes","listen","call","plays"]}]},{"id":7855,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I always <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to music in my car.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["work","listen","drinks","do","cook","goes","go","play","call","plays"]}]},{"id":7856,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>My son <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> football every weekend.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["listen","go","work","cook","drinks","do","play","plays","call","goes"]}]}]},{"id":928,"questions":[{"id":7857,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We _____ dinner at 6 pm.</div>","choices":[{"id":13904,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>plays</span>"},{"id":13905,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>read</span>"},{"id":13906,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>studies</span>"},{"id":13907,"letter":"D.","html":"<span>have</span>"},{"id":13908,"letter":"E.","html":"<span>send</span>"}]},{"i